# AGENTS.md

Instructions for AI coding agents working in this repository.

## Project and current state

BT4012 Fraud Analytics, NUS AY2026/2027 Semester 1. The group presentation and 8-12 page PDF report are due **20 November 2026, 23:59 (Asia/Singapore)** and together account for 35% of the course grade.

Use `BT4012_Proposal_BAF_Revised.pdf` and `feedback.md` as current research context. The revised proposal studies bank account fraud detection under temporal drift and class imbalance using BAF. Lecturer feedback calls for matched-size recent-versus-historical comparisons and model-specific feature/preprocessing justification. The supplied feedback ends mid-sentence; do not reconstruct the missing text.

BAF Base (Kaggle version 2) is the first-study variant, at ignored `data/raw/baf/Base.csv`. The implemented study is specified by `docs/experiment-protocol.md` and `configs/study.json`, with modules under `baf/`. It uses development months 0-6 and a frozen month-7 evaluation. Refer to OpenSpec tasks and `reports/baf-study-v1/` for verified completion and measured outputs. Settings are analyst-selected and open to group review. `archive/` contains ignored historical planning documents and the course brief; a fresh clone does not include these. IBM AML and archived BAF alternatives are historical context.

The first study completed 90 validation, 14 final and three diagnostic fits. Read `reports/baf-study-v1/findings.md` for measured conclusions and limitations. Month 7 has already been consumed; preserve the existing source/config and selection hashes for this run. Changes to the modelling protocol require a separate exploratory study configuration and cannot restore an independent month-7 holdout.

The separate improvement study is complete under `configs/improvements.json`, `docs/improvement-protocol.md` and `baf/improvements.py`. It adds 51 forward fits, nine validation blends, three adaptive development-only logistic diagnostic fits, five exploratory month-7 model fits and two selected blends. `reports/baf-improvements-v1/findings.md` reports multiple operating policies and the measured ensemble/linear-feature gains with conditional uncertainty. The raw-C=0.1 diagnostic is configured separately and excluded from main selection and month 7. Preserve this study's frozen sources/config/software identity too; further tuning requires a new study. These settings remain analyst-selected, not approved group decisions.

