- Read `openspec/config.yaml`, relevant `openspec/specs/*/spec.md` and any active change before substantial work.
- Use the generated `.agents/skills/openspec-*/` workflows for proposals, experiments, pipeline changes and changes to evaluation behaviour. Routine typo fixes need no new change.
- Keep proposed requirements in `openspec/changes/<change>/specs/`; main specs describe current requirements. Archive after the tasks and their outputs are verified.
- `define-baf-experiment-protocol` tracks the documented protocol; `run-baf-eda-and-hypothesis-tests` tracks execution and findings. Artifact completion is different from task completion.
- `improve-baf-detection` tracks the completed exploratory improvement study and its adaptive controlled logistic diagnostic.
- Preserve the frozen selection and test-access record. After month 7 has been scored, describe it as an already-consumed holdout; do not retune on it and claim fresh confirmation.
- Mark tasks complete only after their actual outputs exist and have been checked. Do not invent results or treat unselected settings as group decisions.
- Keep this file, `README.md`, project context and relevant specs consistent. Do not rewrite archived historical documents to make them current.
- Run `openspec validate --all --strict --no-interactive` after editing OpenSpec artifacts.

## Research and implementation conventions

- Prefer chronological train/validation/test splits; all compared strategies must predict the same future applications. Any random split is a labelled diagnostic benchmark, not evidence of drift by itself.
- Separate recency from training size with matched-K historical controls; state whether class proportions are also controlled. Fit preprocessing and select models/thresholds using eligible training/validation data only.
- Document actual variables, feature roles, categorical/missing-value handling and differences between logistic regression and tree preprocessing.
- Freeze choices before final test evaluation. Report imbalance-appropriate metrics and precision/recall at fixed review capacity, plus missed fraud and legitimate applications flagged.
- Add concrete reproduction instructions to `README.md` with modelling code: dependencies, data access, configurations, execution order, seeds and outputs.
- Do not commit large raw datasets. Use ignored `data/` and `outputs/` for local inputs and run artifacts.

## Deliverables

The report must be 8-12 pages excluding references/appendices and follow: Problem Description -> Data Overview -> Methodology -> Experiments and Results -> Conclusion. The full brief is locally at `archive/BT4012 Project Guidelines and Grading Criteria.pdf`.

Acknowledge generative AI assistance, external code and public notebooks in the report, and keep submitted work explainable by the group. Track assistance sources as substantive work is produced.
